  "Question": "Consider the operation \\(*\\) defined by the following table:\n\n\\[\\begin{array}{c|cccc} * & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\hline 1 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\end{array}\\]\n\nFor example, \\(3 * 2 = 1.\\) Then \\((2 * 4) * (1 * 3) =\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "For each operation, use the row labeled by the first number and the column labeled by the second. Work inside the parentheses first. The table gives\n\\[2*4=3,\\qquad1*3=3.\\]\nSubstitute these results, then look up the entry in row \\(3\\), column \\(3\\):\n\\[(2*4)*(1*3)=3*3=4.\\]\nThe answer is \\(4\\), choice \\(\\mathrm D\\).",
